  "details": "Currently the only way to see what \"Version\" the Avatar you're uploading is, is through the SDK Builder Panel.\n\nI think this should be actually used in-game, with a line added in your Avatar Details showing what the Version Number of your Avatar is returning.\n\nIn addition, I would like to see a feature where it would be possible to make that same version number be inserted automatically in your Avatar's Name (at the user's discretion) through a text argument in the SDK Builder Panel. Something like <!version>, which would insert the Avatar Version number in place of that argument.\n\nExample: An Avatar named \"Dragon v1.0.<!version>\" that has the Version 4 in the SDK, would return as \"Dragon v1.0.4\" in-game.",
